From 42de753fee0e5d4513836d5b424c2663f659c139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 06:10:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: series replay keeps CR (--keep-cr); evidence
 receipts restored to their original LF bytes

The -text renormalize took the CRLF checkout bytes as the blob, turning LF receipts into CRLF
blobs that git am (which strips CR by default) could never reproduce. Receipts are back to the
LF bytes their tools wrote; replay now applies with --keep-cr and core.autocrlf=false so any
future byte-exact receipt survives the round trip.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - HQ seat-58 root fix for replay parity
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - tooling and evidence bytes
Lane: lane-233
